1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:00,920
Hello, everyone!

2
00:00:00,960 --> 00:00:02,880
The livestreaming of J Weekly
and the Rehab Club's

3
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:05,800
charity fundraising Static Apnea Challenge
will now begin.

4
00:00:05,880 --> 00:00:07,040
Without further ado,

5
00:00:07,160 --> 00:00:08,960
Jarvis is ready to inhale pure oxygen,

6
00:00:09,080 --> 00:00:11,240
the Static Apnea Challenge will soon begin.

7
00:01:30,240 --> 00:01:32,560
(Three months after the incident)

8
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:37,400
Jarvis...

9
00:01:37,440 --> 00:01:38,760
Get up! Enough horsing around...

10
00:01:38,840 --> 00:01:40,160
Get up, Jarvis...

11
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:41,240
Hey, are you OK?

12
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:45,680
Gogo Sir...still looking at the case
from three months ago?

13
00:01:45,800 --> 00:01:47,760
I still can't figure it out.

14
00:01:47,960 --> 00:01:51,360
Relax! It's lunchtime. Let's go eat.

15
00:01:54,120 --> 00:01:56,160
Are you OK, Wu Sir?

16
00:01:56,280 --> 00:01:58,280
What are you laughing at?

17
00:01:58,440 --> 00:02:01,360
This clip is hilarious...

18
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:02,720
(Neighbor Vs stink bomb)

19
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:03,840
It's me again, Agent J.

20
00:02:03,960 --> 00:02:05,200
Today's game is very simple.

21
00:02:05,320 --> 00:02:06,320
We have two gas cylinders.

22
00:02:06,480 --> 00:02:07,760
Pick one and take a whiff.

23
00:02:07,840 --> 00:02:08,640
One is oxygen.

24
00:02:08,760 --> 00:02:11,200
The other is...more than that.

25
00:02:11,440 --> 00:02:14,280
Agent J Channel?

26
00:02:16,960 --> 00:02:18,880
What did you give me? It stinks!

27
00:02:18,920 --> 00:02:20,880
Relax! It's just a stink bomb.

28
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:23,560
J Weekly had a Static Apnea Challenge before

29
00:02:23,720 --> 00:02:26,000
they meant to use one of these
to trick one of their own.

30
00:02:26,280 --> 00:02:28,280
Hold on. Rewind that.

31
00:02:28,360 --> 00:02:29,360
I want to listen again.

32
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:31,280
J Weekly had an Static Apnea
Challenge before

33
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:32,880
they meant to use one of these
to trick one of their own.

34
00:02:33,040 --> 00:02:33,840
That's it!

35
00:02:34,040 --> 00:02:35,760
Using the stink bomb on their own staff

36
00:02:35,920 --> 00:02:38,480
was never disclosed to the public.

37
00:02:38,640 --> 00:02:39,600
What does that mean?

38
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:40,880
It means this Agent J

39
00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:43,120
is connected to the livestreaming of the
Static Apnea Challenge three months ago.

40
00:02:43,280 --> 00:02:44,440
What other clips does he have?

41
00:02:44,720 --> 00:02:45,840
Who's the moderator?

42
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,160
They never show their faces.

43
00:02:48,320 --> 00:02:50,120
What about the Static Apnea Challenge?

44
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:52,400
Three months ago, I was at an exchange
with the Mainland Police.

45
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:53,360
I missed it.

46
00:02:53,520 --> 00:02:56,320
The case was connected to J Weekly.

47
00:02:58,760 --> 00:03:00,840
Three months ago, all their videos

48
00:03:00,960 --> 00:03:03,000
were about pulling pranks on people.

49
00:03:05,680 --> 00:03:07,560
What's going on?

50
00:03:09,880 --> 00:03:11,040
Yeah!

51
00:03:11,280 --> 00:03:13,520
Keep it up...

52
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:16,960
Please take off your jacket.

53
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:20,640
Sorry! This is a routine check.

54
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:21,840
I'm in a hurry!

55
00:03:23,880 --> 00:03:26,560
Run, Tom! Run!

56
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:29,440
Hurry...run!

57
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:30,800
The J Weekly Channel,

58
00:03:30,920 --> 00:03:32,160
was quite a hit a year ago.

59
00:03:32,320 --> 00:03:33,840
It went viral after Wendy showed up.

60
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:34,880
(Little J Media)

61
00:03:34,960 --> 00:03:35,920
Who are you?

62
00:03:36,040 --> 00:03:38,080
I'm Wendy, your diehard fan.

63
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:40,440
Jarvis, you're so amazing!

64
00:03:40,600 --> 00:03:41,840
I've been following you for a long time.

65
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:42,960
Can we help you?

66
00:03:43,080 --> 00:03:44,120
I want to join you.

67
00:03:44,360 --> 00:03:45,760
Join us?

68
00:03:45,960 --> 00:03:47,840
What are your strengths?

69
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:49,280
I'm pure and true.

70
00:03:49,440 --> 00:03:51,600
More importantly, I really care

71
00:03:51,720 --> 00:03:53,360
and I enjoy pulling pranks.

72
00:03:53,440 --> 00:03:55,040
It's not as easy as you think.

73
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:56,120
You must use your head.

74
00:03:56,880 --> 00:03:59,200
The case started with Wendy on a trampoline.

75
00:03:59,320 --> 00:04:01,360
You have a dog and it went missing.
How can you find it?

76
00:04:01,480 --> 00:04:04,080
Call the Police? Dial 999?

77
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:05,200
Wrong!

78
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:07,520
The answer is dye your hair blonde.

79
00:04:07,640 --> 00:04:09,200
Because it's a golden retriever.

80
00:04:09,400 --> 00:04:12,160
Go to Hell!

81
00:04:21,480 --> 00:04:22,200
Are you OK?

82
00:04:22,360 --> 00:04:23,200
Are you OK?

83
00:04:23,400 --> 00:04:25,520
I'm fine...I'd rather kill myself

84
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:27,360
than answer your dumb IQ questions.

85
00:04:27,840 --> 00:04:29,200
(Three months ago)

86
00:04:29,280 --> 00:04:34,240
Up...

87
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:42,640
Today, the Fake Metal Detector prank
reached 500K views!

88
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:44,160
Yeah!

89
00:04:44,280 --> 00:04:46,400
It's not only in the top spot,

90
00:04:46,600 --> 00:04:49,600
it also broke our channel record.

91
00:04:49,720 --> 00:04:51,040
Yeah!

92
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:53,760
This "cup" is your award.

93
00:04:53,920 --> 00:04:58,200
Mr. Tsang Chun-kit, the Fake Metal Detector
broke the 500K viewership,

94
00:04:58,360 --> 00:05:00,320
how do you feel about that?

95
00:05:04,080 --> 00:05:07,600
I would like to thank a fellow moron,

96
00:05:07,720 --> 00:05:11,040
my partner in crime, Paul.

97
00:05:11,200 --> 00:05:15,040
This moron is not only my co-host,

98
00:05:15,120 --> 00:05:16,960
we were up all night brainstorming.

99
00:05:17,080 --> 00:05:19,520
It was his idea.

100
00:05:19,640 --> 00:05:22,160
He deserves this "cup" as well.

101
00:05:22,360 --> 00:05:23,040
OK...

102
00:05:23,200 --> 00:05:24,720
Hung Tzi-long, your partner thanked you.

103
00:05:24,920 --> 00:05:25,760
Say something.

104
00:05:25,920 --> 00:05:29,040
I also wish to thank this moron, Tom.

105
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:31,440
To be able to work with
such a talented moron,

106
00:05:31,640 --> 00:05:33,600
the pleasure is all mine, moron!

107
00:05:37,400 --> 00:05:39,520
Cheers!

108
00:05:40,760 --> 00:05:42,320
Hey, don't drink from the bottle.

109
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:43,200
What about us?

110
00:05:43,320 --> 00:05:44,400
You want to drink this?

111
00:05:44,480 --> 00:05:45,280
Go ahead!

112
00:05:45,400 --> 00:05:47,760
On this happy occasion, let's take a selfie.

113
00:05:48,280 --> 00:05:52,000
Wait...don't forget our linchpin,
Auntie Ching.

114
00:05:52,160 --> 00:05:53,680
Auntie Ching!

115
00:05:54,200 --> 00:05:57,280
We won't be here without Auntie Ching.

116
00:05:57,400 --> 00:06:01,600
Me? I'm just your cleaning lady.

117
00:06:01,680 --> 00:06:03,520
Of course you can do without me.

118
00:06:03,640 --> 00:06:06,000
But not without your sweet soup.

119
00:06:06,160 --> 00:06:08,880
We'd be dead if we pull an all-nighter
without it.

120
00:06:09,360 --> 00:06:11,200
There's more.

121
00:06:11,400 --> 00:06:15,120
We'll never forget her special recipe...

122
00:06:15,320 --> 00:06:17,200
...Braised chicken wings.

123
00:06:17,360 --> 00:06:18,800
Say no more, let's take a picture.

124
00:06:18,960 --> 00:06:19,920
Yes!

125
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:22,200
1...2...3...another one!

126
00:06:22,360 --> 00:06:25,760
Go ahead, I'll go clean up.

127
00:06:25,920 --> 00:06:26,640
OK!

128
00:06:27,920 --> 00:06:28,640
Again.

129
00:06:28,800 --> 00:06:30,520
Did you forget something?

130
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:31,360
You want to be in the center?

131
00:06:31,520 --> 00:06:33,360
OK...come on!
Yes!

132
00:06:33,800 --> 00:06:35,400
Jarvis, you're back!

133
00:06:35,640 --> 00:06:37,920
Popping the champagne without me?

134
00:06:38,040 --> 00:06:39,040
What are we celebrating?

135
00:06:39,080 --> 00:06:42,240
Tom and Paul's Fake Metal Detector

136
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:44,480
just hit the 500K mark

137
00:06:44,560 --> 00:06:45,680
and set a new record.

138
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:47,080
Not bad.

139
00:06:47,200 --> 00:06:49,840
But only because you, the master of pranks
were leading them,

140
00:06:49,960 --> 00:06:51,280
that's why they did so well.

141
00:06:51,400 --> 00:06:52,520
You should get the credit.

142
00:06:53,080 --> 00:06:54,480
Wendy is right.

143
00:06:54,560 --> 00:06:56,480
Without you leading us

144
00:06:56,600 --> 00:06:58,400
and giving our video the final touch,

145
00:06:58,520 --> 00:07:00,160
we couldn't have done it.

146
00:07:00,280 --> 00:07:03,840
Little J Media has a pool of talent.

147
00:07:03,960 --> 00:07:05,440
Thanks to Tom and Paul,

148
00:07:05,520 --> 00:07:07,280
who set a new record for us.

149
00:07:07,400 --> 00:07:11,760
We also have our diehard fan Wendy,

150
00:07:13,040 --> 00:07:19,360
and also Modem...and Peter.

151
00:07:19,760 --> 00:07:21,680
As long as we stay united,

152
00:07:21,840 --> 00:07:25,520
J Weekly will be Hong Kong's top channel.

153
00:07:26,360 --> 00:07:29,600
Cheers...

154
00:07:33,400 --> 00:07:34,400
Close the door!

155
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:45,880
Good job, 500K hits.

156
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:47,200
You popped the champagne without me.

157
00:07:47,360 --> 00:07:48,400
Are you slighting me?

158
00:07:48,520 --> 00:07:50,400
I forgot. Sorry!

159
00:07:50,480 --> 00:07:52,640
Did you forget how you ended up here?

160
00:07:52,800 --> 00:07:53,760
(Two years ago)

161
00:07:53,840 --> 00:07:54,880
Hey!

162
00:07:55,200 --> 00:07:56,400
Did you get the letter?

163
00:07:56,520 --> 00:07:59,840
Yeah, we're now extras.

164
00:07:59,960 --> 00:08:01,920
Are we that bad?

165
00:08:02,160 --> 00:08:07,920
Even five shows a year can't put
food on the table.

166
00:08:08,080 --> 00:08:11,600
Switching us to extras is like firing us.

167
00:08:11,760 --> 00:08:12,880
Right!

168
00:08:13,080 --> 00:08:15,760
This has a nice view.

169
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:17,440
Pick a spot and get ready to camp out here.

170
00:08:17,600 --> 00:08:18,160
Good idea!

171
00:08:18,280 --> 00:08:20,480
Gentlemen, do you have time...

172
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:23,600
Are you Tsang Chun-kit?

173
00:08:23,760 --> 00:08:24,920
You know me?

174
00:08:25,040 --> 00:08:27,040
Of course! You work at the TV station.

175
00:08:27,160 --> 00:08:28,680
I see you on TV all the time.

176
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:30,160
He's quite good.

177
00:08:30,280 --> 00:08:31,520
Nice to meet you.

178
00:08:31,640 --> 00:08:33,600
Since you're not busy.

179
00:08:33,760 --> 00:08:35,520
Let's play a game.

180
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:38,320
Here's $2,000.

181
00:08:38,520 --> 00:08:41,600
If you win, the money is yours.

182
00:08:43,800 --> 00:08:45,920
We hit rock bottom back then.

183
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:48,960
Thanks for bringing us on board

184
00:08:49,160 --> 00:08:50,640
and giving us a chance as a host

185
00:08:50,760 --> 00:08:52,240
so we can get some exposure.

186
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:54,560
And how to shoot, edit and brainstorm.

187
00:08:54,680 --> 00:08:56,400
Didn't I teach you everything?

188
00:08:56,640 --> 00:08:58,720
You made us what we are today.

189
00:08:59,400 --> 00:09:01,120
When we first started the channel,

190
00:09:01,280 --> 00:09:03,040
the three of us had to do everything.

191
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:04,640
We didn't mind the hard work and
charged ahead.

192
00:09:04,720 --> 00:09:07,120
We went up the river and got us
where we are today.

193
00:09:07,240 --> 00:09:09,120
You know why we're still here?

194
00:09:09,320 --> 00:09:10,960
Because of what's here!

195
00:09:11,120 --> 00:09:15,040
An online channel is not just
about viewership.

196
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:19,280
You must know what kind of content
will prompt viewers to top up.

197
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:23,200
The key is the money goes
directly to the channel.

198
00:09:23,400 --> 00:09:25,680
I don't care what you do,

199
00:09:25,800 --> 00:09:30,400
I want content that will ensure tipping.

200
00:09:30,600 --> 00:09:33,040
Just like Wendy on the Trampoline,

201
00:09:33,160 --> 00:09:35,680
that kind of video is like gold.

202
00:09:35,800 --> 00:09:38,000
Don't shoot whatever you like.

203
00:09:38,240 --> 00:09:40,880
What sort of video has high gold content?

204
00:09:41,360 --> 00:09:44,880
Open your eyes and look around!

205
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:47,600
Wendy is the key to our fortune.

206
00:09:47,720 --> 00:09:50,240
What do you have?

207
00:09:55,280 --> 00:09:56,560
Pull the prank on her.

208
00:09:57,120 --> 00:09:59,680
She already injured herself last time.

209
00:09:59,800 --> 00:10:00,880
You're sure about this?

210
00:10:00,960 --> 00:10:04,920
She's one of us and your diehard fan.

211
00:10:05,040 --> 00:10:06,560
Let's think of something else.

212
00:10:06,720 --> 00:10:08,480
That's the reality.

213
00:10:08,680 --> 00:10:10,240
Whenever we run anything on Wendy,

214
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:11,840
the top-up rate is 50% more.

215
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:13,760
More than what you get
for both of your videos.

216
00:10:13,920 --> 00:10:14,560
No, but you...

217
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:16,880
You have a problem?

218
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:20,160
OK, if Yat Wong Entertainment
has a problem with your video,

219
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:22,240
you better explain to Mr. Tsui.

220
00:10:43,280 --> 00:10:46,560
Are we really going after Wendy?

221
00:10:46,720 --> 00:10:48,400
This isn't the first time.

222
00:10:48,560 --> 00:10:51,920
Wendy's known to be a goofball

223
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:53,760
and easy prey.

224
00:10:53,880 --> 00:10:56,400
But this guy is heartless
to victimize a team member.

225
00:10:56,560 --> 00:11:01,280
He's known to be a scumbag.

226
00:11:01,400 --> 00:11:04,720
He's obviously jealous of us.

227
00:11:04,800 --> 00:11:07,040
Our videos have higher hit rates than his.

228
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:10,240
That's why he pressured us
about the tipping.

229
00:11:10,360 --> 00:11:11,280
He's so cheap.

230
00:11:11,440 --> 00:11:13,280
Now that he's a KOL,

231
00:11:13,440 --> 00:11:15,760
he's afraid we may surpass him.

232
00:11:15,880 --> 00:11:21,360
Wait...why should we bother?

233
00:11:21,480 --> 00:11:24,400
We have always shot and edited
our own videos,

234
00:11:24,520 --> 00:11:26,720
let's just stick to our plan

235
00:11:26,880 --> 00:11:29,800
and we'll get back at him with hit rates.

236
00:11:29,920 --> 00:11:30,880
Good!

237
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:32,560
Let's fine tune our idea

238
00:11:32,720 --> 00:11:34,160
and try to get more noise.

239
00:11:34,600 --> 00:11:38,160
Wendy, we're shooting the Blind Gourmet,

240
00:11:38,280 --> 00:11:39,360
if you give us the wrong answer,

241
00:11:39,520 --> 00:11:42,080
the basin of water will pour on you. OK?

242
00:11:42,280 --> 00:11:43,440
That's it?

243
00:11:43,600 --> 00:11:46,560
The huge basin will have quite an impact.

244
00:11:46,720 --> 00:11:50,640
Will Jarvis approve of this?

245
00:11:50,760 --> 00:11:51,520
That's fine.

246
00:11:51,560 --> 00:11:52,720
You're all covered up!

247
00:11:52,800 --> 00:11:54,000
Is this a children's program?

248
00:11:54,160 --> 00:11:55,280
I agree.

249
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:56,720
See? Even the model is complaining.

250
00:11:56,880 --> 00:11:58,640
You need to do some introspection.

251
00:11:58,920 --> 00:12:01,600
Put this on...

252
00:12:03,400 --> 00:12:04,720
Instant hit.

253
00:12:05,040 --> 00:12:06,480
It's practically see-through.

254
00:12:06,640 --> 00:12:09,280
Jarvis, the basin of water is just
warming up.

255
00:12:09,400 --> 00:12:10,600
The best is yet to come.

256
00:12:10,640 --> 00:12:13,120
We saved the big punishment for later.

257
00:12:13,240 --> 00:12:15,280
I want noise from start to finish.

258
00:12:15,480 --> 00:12:17,040
Or else who'd want to watch?

259
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:18,800
No one till top up.

260
00:12:19,360 --> 00:12:22,160
Wendy, you know what I mean?

261
00:12:22,320 --> 00:12:24,480
Right! You want impact.

262
00:12:24,600 --> 00:12:26,160
I'll change into that later.

263
00:12:27,640 --> 00:12:28,720
Go get ready.

264
00:12:28,840 --> 00:12:29,520
Right!

265
00:12:29,560 --> 00:12:30,480
Peter!

266
00:12:32,360 --> 00:12:35,680
You won't manage. I'll do it myself.

267
00:12:44,800 --> 00:12:46,720
What is it, Auntie Ching?

268
00:12:46,800 --> 00:12:49,280
Am I in your way?

269
00:12:49,360 --> 00:12:50,720
No, go ahead.

270
00:12:51,120 --> 00:12:54,720
I'm just being nosy.

271
00:12:54,840 --> 00:13:02,080
Are you really going to wear
what Jarvis gave you?

272
00:13:02,920 --> 00:13:05,200
It won't be just that.

273
00:13:05,320 --> 00:13:07,120
I'll wear something else.

274
00:13:07,280 --> 00:13:08,880
Still!

275
00:13:09,120 --> 00:13:12,000
For you to wear something like that

276
00:13:12,120 --> 00:13:15,440
in front of the camera...

277
00:13:15,560 --> 00:13:17,440
You don't mind?

278
00:13:17,600 --> 00:13:19,520
To get more traffic for the channel

279
00:13:19,760 --> 00:13:21,920
and I can get more exposure.

280
00:13:22,080 --> 00:13:24,720
If Jarvis thinks using me has an impact,

281
00:13:24,840 --> 00:13:26,720
I must help him out.

282
00:13:26,920 --> 00:13:28,400
You're very young,

283
00:13:28,520 --> 00:13:30,880
naturally, you'd want to do your best.

284
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:37,360
But Jarvis often carries something too far.

285
00:13:37,560 --> 00:13:40,200
Not to mention you hurt yourself last time.

286
00:13:40,280 --> 00:13:44,080
Jarvis has vision.

287
00:13:44,160 --> 00:13:47,120
He knows what's best for Little J Media.

288
00:13:47,800 --> 00:13:52,000
Just remember, at the right moment,

289
00:13:52,080 --> 00:13:53,920
you must protect yourself.

290
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:56,560
I know what I'm doing.

291
00:13:59,560 --> 00:14:01,920
Don't ask me. Ask Modem and Peter.

292
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:03,360
They're behind the camera.

293
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:08,320
Wendy, don't tell me
you're wearing that underneath.

294
00:14:08,440 --> 00:14:09,760
Just put this on.

295
00:14:09,840 --> 00:14:12,720
That's no different from being naked.

296
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:15,040
Relax! We'll use forced perspective
when we shoot.

297
00:14:16,280 --> 00:14:19,040
Stop standing there! Go change!

298
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:24,080
Mr. Tsui!

299
00:14:24,200 --> 00:14:25,840
Jarvis, can you take a break?

300
00:14:25,920 --> 00:14:27,120
We need to talk.

301
00:14:27,360 --> 00:14:28,400
We're about to do a livestreaming.

302
00:14:28,520 --> 00:14:29,360
Let me do this first.

303
00:14:29,520 --> 00:14:31,520
Stop the livestreaming. We need to talk now.

304
00:14:31,600 --> 00:14:32,480
In my room.

305
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:39,680
Ngai Ka-yan, get in here.

306
00:14:46,720 --> 00:14:48,560
Well? Shall we go ahead?

307
00:14:48,680 --> 00:14:52,800
Mr. Tsui is the boss. Pack up and change.

308
00:14:58,320 --> 00:15:00,480
Tom, you look so smug.

309
00:15:00,640 --> 00:15:02,640
Did you ask Mr. Tsui to drop by?

310
00:15:03,320 --> 00:15:06,720
Tom, I didn't expect you to come to me
behind Jarvis' back.

311
00:15:06,840 --> 00:15:11,200
You know Little J is a subsidiary of
Yat Wong,

312
00:15:11,320 --> 00:15:14,960
and I give Jarvis a free rein of
what to shoot.

313
00:15:15,160 --> 00:15:18,880
But Jarvis is getting out of hand
just to get noise.

314
00:15:19,080 --> 00:15:20,880
He didn't care Wendy was hurt

315
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:22,480
and insisted we use her again.

316
00:15:22,680 --> 00:15:24,320
I can no longer put up with it.

317
00:15:24,480 --> 00:15:26,240
That's why I came to you.

318
00:15:26,320 --> 00:15:27,920
From a business perspective,

319
00:15:28,040 --> 00:15:30,720
Jarvis is making money for the company

320
00:15:30,880 --> 00:15:34,000
and advertisers trust him.

321
00:15:34,160 --> 00:15:38,000
To put it nicely, I'm in charge of Little J.

322
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:43,440
But Jarvis actually calls the shots.

323
00:15:44,920 --> 00:15:50,720
Hegemony is not exactly healthy
for the company.

324
00:15:50,880 --> 00:15:53,760
Perhaps, I can be useful to you.

325
00:15:55,800 --> 00:15:57,200
Jarvis, what are you doing?

326
00:15:57,360 --> 00:15:58,240
We don't want anything cheap.

327
00:15:58,400 --> 00:16:00,320
If we have no viewers, we have no money.

328
00:16:00,440 --> 00:16:01,520
Use your head!

329
00:16:11,200 --> 00:16:13,360
I finished editing.

330
00:16:13,440 --> 00:16:15,440
Let me know if you have a problem.

331
00:16:15,520 --> 00:16:19,280
Are you in a hurry? Watch it with me.

332
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:22,160
(J Weekly)

333
00:16:22,280 --> 00:16:22,640
(Correct Ways to Use a Wheelchair)

334
00:16:22,840 --> 00:16:23,680
I'm helping you...

335
00:16:23,840 --> 00:16:25,920
Are you OK?

336
00:16:26,080 --> 00:16:27,280
Thanks.
Get up...

337
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:28,680
Thank you.

338
00:16:28,720 --> 00:16:30,000
Come on...

339
00:16:31,720 --> 00:16:33,360
What's wrong with you?

340
00:16:33,520 --> 00:16:36,400
You're a wimp, pal. Have you eaten?

341
00:16:36,560 --> 00:16:37,760
You can walk?

342
00:16:37,920 --> 00:16:39,280
Who says I can't?

343
00:16:39,400 --> 00:16:40,200
You played me for a fool!

344
00:16:40,280 --> 00:16:42,480
Look over there, big guy!

345
00:16:42,640 --> 00:16:43,600
Over here...

346
00:16:43,720 --> 00:16:45,680
Hello, you're on J Weekly...

347
00:16:45,760 --> 00:16:47,800
I can't believe after working
with me for so long,

348
00:16:47,960 --> 00:16:50,160
the end product is so raw.

349
00:16:50,520 --> 00:16:55,080
Yes, it's raw but viewers love this stuff.

350
00:16:55,240 --> 00:16:57,920
The simplest and most direct way
to make people laugh

351
00:16:58,040 --> 00:16:59,840
is considered a hit.

352
00:17:00,080 --> 00:17:02,160
I'm curious...

353
00:17:02,360 --> 00:17:03,920
remember what I taught you

354
00:17:04,040 --> 00:17:05,800
about the objective of these pranks?

355
00:17:05,880 --> 00:17:09,200
The nature of laughing is misfortune.

356
00:17:09,280 --> 00:17:11,880
We laugh when we see
the misfortune of others.

357
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:13,920
You said you like to shoot these pranks

358
00:17:14,080 --> 00:17:16,720
because if the misfortune of someone
is only known to one person,

359
00:17:16,840 --> 00:17:18,320
then it's truly unfortunate.

360
00:17:18,400 --> 00:17:19,760
But if we can record it

361
00:17:19,920 --> 00:17:21,280
and make other people laugh,

362
00:17:21,400 --> 00:17:24,480
sharing the laughter is considered a merit.

363
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:26,720
We should not waste a good laugh.

364
00:17:26,840 --> 00:17:28,400
You still remember?

365
00:17:28,600 --> 00:17:30,880
There's no need to imitate me.

366
00:17:31,840 --> 00:17:34,840
Viewers' tastes have changed.

367
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:39,080
They want to see something exciting
and sensational.

368
00:17:39,240 --> 00:17:43,080
I agree we need to adjust to
the viewers' tastes,

369
00:17:43,200 --> 00:17:44,960
but I stick to my bottomline,

370
00:17:45,080 --> 00:17:47,880
of nobody getting hurt.

371
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:49,320
You're right.

372
00:17:49,440 --> 00:17:51,360
You're beginning to have your own thinking.

373
00:17:51,480 --> 00:17:53,280
OK...here's your chance.

374
00:17:53,360 --> 00:17:54,800
If this piece really worked,

375
00:17:54,960 --> 00:17:57,920
I won't interfere with any ideas
you and Paul come up with anymore.

376
00:18:00,360 --> 00:18:01,920
Don't look so shocked.

377
00:18:02,200 --> 00:18:03,800
I'm telling you now,

378
00:18:04,160 --> 00:18:07,680
I'll let you run your own channel.

379
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:10,560
Great!

380
00:18:13,160 --> 00:18:14,880
It takes so long to load 20%?

381
00:18:15,040 --> 00:18:16,360
We're dead if we can't upload it today.

382
00:18:16,440 --> 00:18:17,760
Something wrong with the connection?

383
00:18:17,920 --> 00:18:19,360
Connection is fine.

384
00:18:19,520 --> 00:18:21,040
Maybe it's the network in the building.

385
00:18:21,160 --> 00:18:22,280
I need to check.

386
00:18:22,440 --> 00:18:24,800
Crap! We must go on air today.

387
00:18:24,960 --> 00:18:26,320
What's the problem?

388
00:18:26,480 --> 00:18:27,800
We have something to upload,

389
00:18:27,960 --> 00:18:29,520
but there's a problem with the network.

390
00:18:29,640 --> 00:18:32,320
Not something you can fix quickly?

391
00:18:32,440 --> 00:18:35,360
OK, I need you both to attend a meeting
with me at HQ.

392
00:18:35,520 --> 00:18:37,200
We need to upload it, you promised...

393
00:18:37,360 --> 00:18:39,600
I'm good for my word.

394
00:18:39,720 --> 00:18:41,280
Relax! If you can't upload it today,

395
00:18:41,360 --> 00:18:42,480
do it tomorrow.

396
00:18:42,680 --> 00:18:45,080
Let Modem take care of the technical stuff.

397
00:18:45,160 --> 00:18:47,680
I need you for something big. Let's go!

398
00:18:59,760 --> 00:19:01,280
I'm helping you...

399
00:19:01,440 --> 00:19:02,640
When was this uploaded?

400
00:19:02,800 --> 00:19:04,960
The sooner the better.

401
00:19:05,080 --> 00:19:06,040
We have a lot of likes.

402
00:19:06,200 --> 00:19:07,560
People are topping-up too.

403
00:19:07,680 --> 00:19:08,800
Let me check...

404
00:19:11,160 --> 00:19:12,960
What's wrong with you?

405
00:19:13,080 --> 00:19:14,120
You're a wimp, pal. Have you eaten?

406
00:19:14,240 --> 00:19:16,000
Wait...there are a lot of dislikes!

407
00:19:16,080 --> 00:19:16,880
You can walk?
How come?

408
00:19:17,840 --> 00:19:20,080
A host shouldn't talk like that.

409
00:19:20,160 --> 00:19:21,760
That's cruel!

410
00:19:21,960 --> 00:19:24,600
Wait...I only told him to smile
for the camera.

411
00:19:24,760 --> 00:19:26,000
What did I say?

412
00:19:27,680 --> 00:19:29,520
The nature of laughing is misfortune.

413
00:19:29,760 --> 00:19:32,120
We laugh when we see
the misfortune of others.

414
00:19:32,200 --> 00:19:34,400
If the misfortune of someone
is only known to one person,

415
00:19:34,480 --> 00:19:36,240
then it's truly unfortunate.

416
00:19:36,400 --> 00:19:37,680
But if we can record it

417
00:19:37,840 --> 00:19:39,120
and make other people laugh,

418
00:19:39,280 --> 00:19:42,400
sharing the laughter is considered a merit.

419
00:19:42,520 --> 00:19:44,040
We should not waste a good laugh.

420
00:19:44,120 --> 00:19:45,680
Who added this?

421
00:19:45,840 --> 00:19:47,920
You didn't? Then who did?

422
00:19:49,880 --> 00:19:51,520
There's only one possibility.

423
00:19:54,200 --> 00:19:56,160
Speak up! Did you mess with my video?

424
00:19:56,360 --> 00:19:57,640
I'm just doing my job.

425
00:19:57,720 --> 00:20:00,280
I must follow the Boss' order.

426
00:20:04,720 --> 00:20:06,840
Ngai Ka-yan, you set me up?

427
00:20:06,960 --> 00:20:08,480
What are you talking about?

428
00:20:08,640 --> 00:20:10,840
Quit your act! You recorded what I said
the other day.

429
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:12,960
You told them to edit it into my video.

430
00:20:13,920 --> 00:20:15,760
Remember what I taught you

431
00:20:15,880 --> 00:20:17,880
about the objective of these pranks?

432
00:20:22,720 --> 00:20:24,600
You claimed to let me run a new channel.

433
00:20:24,680 --> 00:20:26,480
That was just the bait to set me up.

434
00:20:26,640 --> 00:20:28,400
What are you talking about?

435
00:20:28,480 --> 00:20:29,920
Why would I do that?

436
00:20:30,040 --> 00:20:31,440
Because you're jealous.

437
00:20:31,520 --> 00:20:33,680
You're scared we would surpass you
and replace you.

438
00:20:33,760 --> 00:20:34,720
That's why you're desperate.

439
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:38,400
Replace me? You and what army?

440
00:20:38,560 --> 00:20:40,960
If I'm jealous of talents,

441
00:20:41,040 --> 00:20:43,640
I wouldn't pick up garbage like you

442
00:20:43,720 --> 00:20:46,280
and teach you to shoot and edit videos
and brainstorm.

443
00:20:46,520 --> 00:20:49,680
Now that you can stand on your own feet,

444
00:20:49,760 --> 00:20:51,920
you begin to challenge my ideas

445
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:53,680
and went to Mr. Tsui behind my back.

446
00:20:54,120 --> 00:20:54,880
I did not.

447
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:55,920
No?

448
00:20:56,640 --> 00:20:58,720
Then why would Mr. Tsui drop by

449
00:20:58,800 --> 00:21:00,640
and stop my livestreaming?

450
00:21:00,880 --> 00:21:03,360
You think you're good enough,

451
00:21:03,560 --> 00:21:05,680
I gave you the green light to take charge.

452
00:21:05,880 --> 00:21:07,680
And what happened?

453
00:21:07,920 --> 00:21:09,760
Look at all the dislikes!

454
00:21:09,920 --> 00:21:13,120
That proves you're both useless.

455
00:21:13,760 --> 00:21:16,960
You admit you removed the original video?

456
00:21:17,200 --> 00:21:18,080
Bloody hell...

457
00:21:18,160 --> 00:21:20,560
Calm down...

458
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:25,920
It's Mr. Tsui. Did you call him?

459
00:21:28,440 --> 00:21:29,600
Hello?

460
00:21:29,760 --> 00:21:31,920
Jarvis, a representative from the Rehab Club

461
00:21:32,080 --> 00:21:33,760
called and complained about
the wheelchair video.

462
00:21:33,880 --> 00:21:35,640
Meet me at the Rehab Club.

463
00:21:35,840 --> 00:21:37,600
OK, I'll be right there.

464
00:21:39,600 --> 00:21:42,360
Look what you did, losers!

465
00:21:42,480 --> 00:21:44,360
We have a complaint from the Rehab Club.

466
00:21:44,480 --> 00:21:46,640
Now I need to defend you.

467
00:21:51,520 --> 00:21:53,800
You're coming with me.

468
00:21:53,960 --> 00:21:57,120
Clean up your own mess.

469
00:22:14,160 --> 00:22:18,600
Hello, I'm Lok Hiu-sin, the representative
of the Rehab Club.

470
00:22:18,680 --> 00:22:21,040
I'll cut to the chase.

471
00:22:21,160 --> 00:22:25,200
J Weekly posted a video called
"Correct Ways to Use a Wheelchair",

472
00:22:25,360 --> 00:22:27,840
I received a lot of input from members

473
00:22:27,960 --> 00:22:30,800
claiming the video has
seriously affected them.

474
00:22:31,000 --> 00:22:33,080
I'm sorry this has affected
your organization.

475
00:22:33,160 --> 00:22:37,120
I'd like you to meet our colleagues
Jarvis, Tom and Paul.

476
00:22:37,320 --> 00:22:38,720
They're in charge of this video.

477
00:22:38,920 --> 00:22:42,160
Please let them explain.

478
00:22:42,520 --> 00:22:45,360
Miss Lok, I created J Weekly.

479
00:22:45,480 --> 00:22:48,040
I'm duty bound but it was my fault

480
00:22:48,200 --> 00:22:50,720
I didn't supervise my colleagues properly

481
00:22:50,800 --> 00:22:53,560
and created such inappropriate content.

482
00:22:53,680 --> 00:22:55,800
I will remove the video immediately.

483
00:22:55,960 --> 00:23:00,040
I trust my colleagues did not mean
to offend the physically challenged.

484
00:23:00,200 --> 00:23:04,040
The video was only meant to be entertaining.

485
00:23:04,120 --> 00:23:09,360
I know. You think your pranks are funny.

486
00:23:09,480 --> 00:23:12,160
Because nothing unfortunate happened to you.

487
00:23:12,400 --> 00:23:13,760
But did you realize,

488
00:23:13,880 --> 00:23:15,920
the way you toy with other people's sympathy

489
00:23:16,040 --> 00:23:17,680
when we truly need help,

490
00:23:17,800 --> 00:23:19,320
no one will help us?

491
00:23:21,520 --> 00:23:25,440
Tom, you said the nature of laughing
is misfortune,

492
00:23:25,720 --> 00:23:27,440
if the misfortune is only known
to one person,

493
00:23:27,560 --> 00:23:29,320
then it's truly unfortunate.

494
00:23:29,640 --> 00:23:32,720
But if we can record it and send it out

495
00:23:32,800 --> 00:23:35,200
so more people can see and share it,

496
00:23:35,280 --> 00:23:36,720
then it'll be a hit.

497
00:23:36,840 --> 00:23:41,560
Tell me, taking pleasure in our pain,

498
00:23:41,640 --> 00:23:43,680
is that right?

499
00:23:43,800 --> 00:23:45,320
Miss Lok, the voice over...

500
00:23:45,440 --> 00:23:47,760
Tom, don't bother to explain.

501
00:23:47,880 --> 00:23:49,880
This time you have gone too far.

502
00:23:50,040 --> 00:23:53,920
Miss Lok, about the impact of this video

503
00:23:54,040 --> 00:23:56,160
on your organization and the
physically challenged,

504
00:23:56,440 --> 00:24:04,480
I would like to apologize on behalf
of Little J Media.

505
00:24:14,080 --> 00:24:17,200
I also have a solution to make up
for our mistake.

506
00:24:17,360 --> 00:24:20,480
We'll do a fundraising for the Rehab Club.

507
00:24:21,560 --> 00:24:25,440
We'll apologize in public for the video

508
00:24:25,600 --> 00:24:29,920
and do something for your organization
through the fundraising.

509
00:24:30,120 --> 00:24:32,040
You're good with these pranks.

510
00:24:32,160 --> 00:24:33,200
You know anything about fundraising?

511
00:24:33,360 --> 00:24:34,960
You have nothing to worry about.

512
00:24:35,160 --> 00:24:38,000
Pulling pranks is only one of our means.

513
00:24:38,160 --> 00:24:42,960
Entertainment is what attracts our viewers

514
00:24:43,080 --> 00:24:47,640
but it's usually lacking in
most fundraising events.

515
00:24:47,840 --> 00:24:49,760
You're quite right.

516
00:24:49,880 --> 00:24:51,360
I hope our collaboration

517
00:24:51,520 --> 00:24:53,360
will be beneficial to both parties.

518
00:24:53,480 --> 00:24:56,080
Jarvis, since the fundraising is your idea,

519
00:24:56,240 --> 00:24:57,680
I'm putting you in charge.

520
00:24:57,840 --> 00:24:58,840
I understand.

521
00:24:59,000 --> 00:25:01,200
I will keep an eye on everything

522
00:25:01,360 --> 00:25:05,120
and won't let Mr. Tsui or Miss Lok down.

523
00:25:07,320 --> 00:25:08,880
Are you celebrating tonight?

524
00:25:09,200 --> 00:25:10,400
Probably.

525
00:25:14,240 --> 00:25:17,360
The Rehab Club is a big organization.

526
00:25:17,480 --> 00:25:19,920
You'll get a lot of perks.

527
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:22,160
Let's not get into that.

528
00:25:22,280 --> 00:25:24,960
Charity work is not about perks.

529
00:25:25,160 --> 00:25:28,400
I'll come up with a brilliant idea

530
00:25:28,560 --> 00:25:31,200
and try to raise as much money as possible.

531
00:25:31,440 --> 00:25:32,760
(A few days later)

532
00:25:32,920 --> 00:25:36,400
Folks, you're all participating in
a new project.

533
00:25:36,560 --> 00:25:39,440
Tom and Paul are working on Tricky Ball.

534
00:25:39,560 --> 00:25:41,600
Tricky Ball is suspended indefinitely.

535
00:25:41,760 --> 00:25:43,680
We need to control our costs

536
00:25:43,800 --> 00:25:45,520
and aim for producing high quality content.

537
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:48,960
(Static Apnea Challenge)

538
00:25:50,080 --> 00:25:54,600
A Static Apnea Challenge?
Jarvis, that's amazing!

539
00:25:54,680 --> 00:25:56,240
You have a new idea already.

540
00:25:56,360 --> 00:25:59,880
This will take place underwater.

541
00:26:00,040 --> 00:26:03,360
We'll invite other media to help us
promote the event.

542
00:26:03,480 --> 00:26:06,480
It'll be on a much bigger scale?

543
00:26:06,560 --> 00:26:09,320
It's nothing but a gimmick.

544
00:26:09,520 --> 00:26:10,760
What's the challenge?

545
00:26:10,920 --> 00:26:13,920
